/-- Unified `CoreQDS` First-Class Algorithmic & Structural Combinator Taxonomy (`CoreQDSCombinator` — `QDS-26..28`):
    - `qfoldTree`: divide-and-conquer reversible tree fold (`rev = 1`, `meas = 0`).
    - `qwalkZipper`: coherent Szegedy / coin-flip tree-zipper walk step (`rev = 1`, `meas = 0`).
    - `qsvtBlockEncode`: Quantum Singular Value Transformation polynomial block-encoding (`rev = 1`, `meas = 0`).
    - `qecFaultTolerantLift`: fault-tolerant surface/qLDPC code syndrome extraction & decoding lift (`meas = 1`).
    - `withinApply`: coherent `within { U } apply { V }` conjugation (`U` requires `rev = 1`, `meas = 0`).
    - `hybridFeedback`: classical-quantum feedback loop annotated with its `ExecutionLoopTier` (`rev = 0`, `meas = 1`). -/
inductive CoreQDSCombinator where
  | qfoldTree            : CoreQDSCombinator
  | qwalkZipper          : CoreQDSCombinator
  | qsvtBlockEncode      : CoreQDSCombinator
  | qecFaultTolerantLift : ExecutionLoopTier → CoreQDSCombinator
  | withinApply          : CoreQDSCombinator
  | hybridFeedback       : ExecutionLoopTier → CoreQDSCombinator
  deriving DecidableEq, Repr

/-- Static type-and-effect composition guard across `CoreQDS` combinators (`checkCoreQdsCombinatorCompositionSafe`):
    1. Any combinator requiring an invertible unitary (`qsvtBlockEncode`, `qwalkZipper`, `qfoldTree`, or the `within { U }`
       compute block of `withinApply`, where `requiresInvertibleUnitary = true`) statically forbids nesting a non-invertible
       measurement-bearing `hybridFeedback` (`hasNestedHybridFeedback = true`).
    2. Any combinator invoking neutral-atom AOD shuttling (`requiresAodShuttle = true`) is statically rejected on targets
